  "caveats": [
    "LEVERAGE-REGIME MIX: BDC 150% coverage and non-1940-Act wrappers allow materially more leverage than 1940-Act funds. Fee bases and return volatility are not like-for-like. [typed per product: AMG Pantheon Fund, LLC: 1940-Act asset-coverage limits, Ares Private Markets Fund: 1940-Act asset-coverage limits, Hamilton Lane Private Assets Fund: 1940-Act asset-coverage limits, KKR Private Equity Conglomerate LLC: no 1940-Act leverage limits (34-Act conglomerate), StepStone Private Markets: 1940-Act asset-coverage limits]",
    "LIQUIDITY-LAW MIX: Rule 23c-3 obligations, discretionary tenders, and repurchase plans give different worst-case exit rights. Cadence numbers alone overstate comparability. [by wrapper type: AMG Pantheon Fund, LLC: board-DISCRETIONARY tender offers (nothing compels the next one), Ares Private Markets Fund: board-DISCRETIONARY tender offers (nothing compels the next one), Hamilton Lane Private Assets Fund: board-DISCRETIONARY tender offers (nothing compels the next one), KKR Private Equity Conglomerate LLC: board-discretionary share repurchases, StepStone Private Markets: board-DISCRETIONARY tender offers (nothing compels the next one)]",
    "KKR Private Equity Conglomerate LLC joins under the authorized fallback: its structural twins are Reg D vehicles with no public filings (data/roster_decisions.md - 'The KKR Private Equity Conglomerate LLC ruling'). Cross-wrapper caveats apply."
  ],
